From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Dichev <stefanbdichev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:17:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] core: bound the reconnect and keep what it hands over
 consistent

Review follow-ups for the access-point reconnect:

- Time out a login that gets no answer after 5 s, as the handshake
  already does, so the next access point is tried; bound a reconnect as
  a whole at 30 s, since looking up access points over HTTP has no
  timeout.
- Leave a session that was shut down during a reconnect alone: don't
  apply or cache the new credentials, which could overwrite another
  user's after a Discovery handover.
- Audio-key requests wait while the session reconnects and get their
  full timeout on the new connection; a shutdown ends them.
- A mercury subscription answered on a connection that closed before it
  registered now ends, checked under the lock that sent its request.
- Close the old connection before reconnecting, and batch packet writes
  again with `forward`.
- Tests for each, on tokio's paused clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zyp13aMbmU4XmKnuCPVRb
(cherry picked from commit cab322309739fea3bb971fac4d7673bd3f55f403)
